{"id": "unknown-2026-07-11-004", "date": "2026-07-11", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 28, "weekday": "Sat"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["green_hydrogen_cost", "electrolyzer_capacity"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "The Hydrogen Stream: Pilot project in Iceland shows geothermal-driven H2 could achieve LCOH of $1.75/kg", "content": "<p>Syntholene’s geothermal-integrated SOEC hydrogen platform could produce hydrogen at an estimated $1.75–$2.10/kg, about one-third the cost of comparable unsubsidized green hydrogen in Europe. Its Iceland demonstration facility aims to validate low-emission hydrogen production and support future commercial-scale deployment, while addressing risks such as electricity costs, electrolyzer durability, and capital expenses.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/07/11/the-hydrogen", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/07/11/the-hydrogen-stream-pilot-project-in-iceland-shows-geothermal-driven-h2-could-achieve-lcoh-of-1-75-kg/", "type": "rss"}]}
